prerequisite_recipe
  record_type "meta_recipe"
  issue "1138"
  topic "prerequisite_discovery"
  title "Recover from a missing toolchain instead of stopping at command not found"
  summary "Machine-readable recovery sequence for issue #1138 B6 (plan 06). A nonzero exit is not always a missing compiler, a permission denial is not installation consent, and a successful setup command with a failing postcondition is still missing. Grounded by tests/unit/specification/prerequisite_recipe.rs against the live source, so this file always describes the recovery that actually runs."
  generalization "To recover from any missing prerequisite, instantiate the eight ordered steps below: bind the failure to the call that produced it, observe the platform rather than infer it, look the publisher up through the trusted-source registry, formalize the procedure with its postcondition, prefer the workspace scope, lower the procedure to allowlisted tool calls, retry and re-probe, and retain the recipe rather than the payload."
prerequisite_step_bind_failure
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "1"
  id "bind_failure"
  title "Bind the failure to the call that produced it"
  detail "A nonzero exit is not always a missing compiler; permission denial is not installation consent. The classifier binds the observed exit code and stderr to the prior call and the recipe step it came from, and only exit 127 or an explicit not-found becomes a prerequisite need."
  precondition "a command was run and reported a nonzero exit"
  postcondition "either a PrerequisiteNeed naming one program, or an explicit not-a-prerequisite verdict"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/mod.rs"
prerequisite_step_observe_platform
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "2"
  id "observe_platform"
  title "Observe the platform and the available runtime"
  detail "Observe the missing executable, the host platform and the available runtime or manager in the client workspace. The platform is observed, never inferred from the requested language: a Kotlin task does not imply a JVM host."
  precondition "a PrerequisiteNeed exists"
  postcondition "the need carries an observed Platform"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/probe.rs"
prerequisite_step_look_up_publisher
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "3"
  id "look_up_publisher"
  title "Look the publisher up through the trusted-source registry"
  detail "Ranking is not authority. The search runs over data/seed/sources-registry.lino in registry order for the prerequisite need kind, and data/seed/setup-publishers.lino pins which host is authoritative for which program, so a lookalike host is refused and the refusal is recorded."
  precondition "the need carries an observed Platform"
  postcondition "a candidate procedure with a named source id, or an exhaustion that names every source consulted"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/publisher.rs"
prerequisite_step_formalize_procedure
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "4"
  id "formalize_procedure"
  title "Formalize the procedure with its postcondition"
  detail "The retrieved text becomes ordered steps, each with the location it may write under and the digest the publisher documents. A procedure with no postcondition probe is refused before anything runs, because nothing could then verify it."
  precondition "a candidate procedure was retrieved"
  postcondition "a SetupProcedure whose postcondition is a runnable probe"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/publisher.rs"
prerequisite_step_prefer_workspace_scope
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "5"
  id "prefer_workspace_scope"
  title "Prefer the workspace scope and refuse without a grant"
  detail "Installation is default-deny. The grant names the programs and the root; a step that writes outside that root is refused before execution whatever the fetched text says, and the installed prefix lives under the workspace so the bytes stay disposable."
  precondition "a SetupProcedure with a postcondition exists"
  postcondition "either an install under the workspace root, or a recorded refusal naming the procedure and the grant"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/install.rs"
prerequisite_step_lower_to_tools
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "6"
  id "lower_to_tools"
  title "Lower the procedure to allowlisted tool calls with explicit environment"
  detail "Shell state does not persist between tool calls, so environment bindings are returned explicitly and replayed on every subsequent step rather than exported and hoped for. Every command is checked against the default-deny allowlist before it runs."
  precondition "an install was permitted"
  postcondition "a WorkspaceToolchain whose environment map is returned to the caller"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/install.rs"
prerequisite_step_retry_and_recheck
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "7"
  id "retry_and_recheck"
  title "Re-probe, then retry the original call"
  detail "A successful setup command is not success. Only the postcondition probe returning Present discharges the need; when it does not, the outcome names both observations and the need stays unsatisfied."
  precondition "the procedure's steps ran"
  postcondition "a re-probe verdict, and a retry only when that verdict is Present"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/mod.rs"
prerequisite_step_retain_experience
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "8"
  id "retain_experience"
  title "Retain the recipe, not the payload"
  detail "The installed bytes are disposable; the record is durable. The ledger keeps the source id, the URL, the content id, the postcondition probe and the observed version, so a forgotten toolchain is rediscovered to the same content id and a restart reattaches without re-probing the publisher."
  precondition "a recovery outcome was produced"
  postcondition "one appended toolchain record carrying a rediscover URL and a content id"
  source_file "src/prerequisite/ledger.rs"
